  "notes": "The 2020s mainstream-trap default, and the research's sharpest claim about him is about the 808: \"his 808 writing is a melodic line, not a root pedal\". That is the one parameter this file will not compromise on — `bassline.rhythm` is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.55 over the widest register in this batch (16–36, twenty semitones), with `glideProb` 0.7 and four passing tones, and `bass808.role` is `counter_riff` with `melodicallyIndependent` set. The second claim is a mix one that is still a MIDI fact: the drums sit loud relative to the melody, so `velocityTiers` is raised across all three tiers rather than the melody being written quieter. Harmony is dark but tonal — the two families the research writes out, i–VI–III–VII and i–iv–VI–VII — voiced on guitar, which `timbreHint` names. Drum drop-outs expose that guitar, so `dropOutBeats` runs at 0.75 over four beats. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium; the inferred parameters are the melodic register bounds and `hihat.fill` numbers, which the paragraph gives only as \"dense 32nd/64th rolls\". The third family (i–VII–VI–III) is INFERRED.",
